# Source files are read directly (imported as ESM, hashed, transformed by
# esbuild/Vitest) on whatever OS checks them out. `core.autocrlf=true` is the
# default on Windows dev machines and on GitHub's windows-latest runners, so
# without this, files with a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang (scripts/*.mjs)
# check out with CRLF and fail to parse when imported as a module — Node's
# shebang stripping only special-cases the CLI entry point, not `import`ed
# files — while Linux/macOS CI keeps LF and never sees the bug. Forcing LF
# everywhere keeps every platform checking out the exact same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party build output must round-trip byte-for-byte on every
# platform. `core.autocrlf` is on by default on Windows, so without `-text`
# git rewrites LF→CRLF on checkout here while Ubuntu CI keeps LF — meaning the
# bytes packaged into public/downloads/shamela-bridge.zip would differ between
# a local build and the production one, for a minified bundle nobody should be
# rewriting in the first place. Same reasoning as scripts/lib/javaSourceHash.mjs,
# which normalises line endings before hashing for exactly this reason.
tools/shamela-bridge/vendor/shamela-mcp/dist/index.js -text
tools/shamela-bridge/vendor/shamela-mcp/helper/*.jar  binary

# The bridge's launcher scripts are executed by the OS that unzips them, so
# each keeps the line endings its own shell requires regardless of platform.
tools/shamela-bridge/start-bridge.bat text eol=crlf
tools/shamela-bridge/start-bridge.sh  text eol=lf
